    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1506">

                <pb facs="0971" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg855"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/139.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Simpich.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If Carranza complains that we appealed to Villa please explain to him that we
                    have acted in this case as we have in all others whether the question arose in
                    territory under his control or in territory under Huerta. We have made
                    representations to the local authorities first <pb facs="0972" n="856"
                        xml:id="pg856"/> in the hope of securing immediate action and afterwards to
                    the highest authorities. Villa has consented to allow inspection of Benton’s
                    body and assuming that Carranza will approve of this we are arranging trip but
                    would like specific approval from Carranza and assurance of protection of party
                    which will include British Consul. We still hope that body will be delivered to
                    widow. Assure Carranza that we appreciate the efforts he has made to protect
                    life and property of foreigners.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
